Over two million in Gaza need winter protection amid Israel's aid restrictions: Palestinian minister

More than 2.1 million Palestinians in Gaza face mounting humanitarian risks as winter approaches, with hundreds of thousands of displaced families lacking adequate shelter as Israeli restrictions prevent the delivery of much-needed relief supplies, a Palestinian minister says.

